def execute_tool(call, principal, registry, policy):

    tool = registry.get(call.name)

    if tool is None:
        return {"error": "unknown_tool"}

    arguments = tool.schema.model_validate(
        call.arguments
    )

    decision = policy.authorize(
        principal=principal,
        operation=tool.name,
        arguments=arguments.model_dump()
    )

    if not decision.allowed:
        return {"error": "not_authorized"}

    if decision.requires_approval:
        return {
            "status": "approval_required"
        }

    return tool.execute(
        arguments=arguments,
        principal=principal
    )
```

This is an architectural skeleton. A complete implementation needs authenticated approval references, deadline enforcement, idempotency, audit logging and output restrictions.
